WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.523
This is WealthPlan, our bring-your-own Week 3 use case.

00:00:03.523 --> 00:00:07.046
In Streamlit, an investor supplies a profile, chooses a

00:00:07.046 --> 00:00:10.568
company, sets risk and time horizon, and asks a

00:00:10.568 --> 00:00:14.091
research question. The one-line job is to turn that

00:00:14.091 --> 00:00:17.614
context into a grounded educational plan that combines company

00:00:17.614 --> 00:00:21.137
research, portfolio analysis, goal scenarios, review, and a human

00:00:21.137 --> 00:00:24.659
decision. This is the actual application, not a mockup.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:31.247
This is a multi-agent workflow, not one model calling

00:00:31.247 --> 00:00:35.135
every tool. A supervisor agent receives the request and

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:39.024
selects three bounded specialists: a company research agent, a

00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:42.912
portfolio analysis agent, and a goal planning agent. Each

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:46.800
specialist owns a focused task, bounded tools, and a

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.688
structured result. Shared typed WealthPlan state carries routing, outputs,

00:00:50.688 --> 00:00:54.576
review findings, approval responses, audit events, and write authorization

00:00:54.576 --> 00:00:57.168
without giving any specialist unrestricted control.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:03.524
Generate WealthPlan invokes the LangGraph supervisor. After normalization and

00:01:03.524 --> 00:01:07.181
Pydantic validation, it fans work out with LangGraph Send.

00:01:07.181 --> 00:01:10.838
The research, portfolio, and goal agents run independently and

00:01:10.838 --> 00:01:14.495
may complete in parallel. Each writes a structured result

00:01:14.495 --> 00:01:18.151
into shared state. LangGraph fans those results back in

00:01:18.151 --> 00:01:21.808
at report assembly, sends the combined draft to risk

00:01:21.808 --> 00:01:25.465
review, and pauses at human approval. That supervisor-specialist fan-out

00:01:25.465 --> 00:01:29.121
and fan-in is the core multi-agent pattern. The badges

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:31.966
identify checkpoint memory and the retrieval services.

00:01:34.666 --> 00:01:38.527
The company screen shows two data paths. Historical fundamentals

00:01:38.527 --> 00:01:42.389
come from the SEC Company Facts XBRL API, independent

00:01:42.389 --> 00:01:46.250
of Pinecone. Filing questions use an indexed ten-K corpus:

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.112
embeddings search the LangGraph Pinecone namespace with a ticker

00:01:50.112 --> 00:01:53.974
filter, then Cohere reranks candidates. The five Microsoft passages

00:01:53.974 --> 00:01:57.835
retain filing section, accession, date, ticker, and source URL.

00:02:00.535 --> 00:02:04.213
The portfolio specialist calculates position value, allocation, gains, sector

00:02:04.213 --> 00:02:07.891
exposure, and concentration from fixed holdings and illustrative prices.

00:02:07.891 --> 00:02:11.569
Those numbers are produced by deterministic tools, not invented

00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:15.246
in model prose. The model may explain the result,

00:02:15.246 --> 00:02:18.924
but it does not own the arithmetic. The application

00:02:18.924 --> 00:02:22.602
labels the price basis and highlights concentration so the

00:02:22.602 --> 00:02:24.645
output remains auditable and educational.

00:02:27.345 --> 00:02:31.228
The goal specialist projects the retirement target and compares

00:02:31.228 --> 00:02:35.111
four, six, and eight percent return assumptions. Inputs such

00:02:35.111 --> 00:02:38.994
as savings, contribution, inflation, withdrawal rate, and retirement age

00:02:38.994 --> 00:02:42.877
remain visible. The tool explicitly warns that these are

00:02:42.877 --> 00:02:46.760
scenarios, not forecasts, and that taxes, fees, volatility, and

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.780
sequence-of-returns risk are outside this deterministic prototype.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.866
After report assembly, policy checks verify specialist completion, narrative

00:02:56.866 --> 00:03:01.251
presence, deterministic calculations, data labels, and no write before

00:03:01.251 --> 00:03:05.637
approval. LangGraph interrupt then pauses. Reads and calculations are

00:03:05.637 --> 00:03:10.022
autonomous, but a consequential approved record requires a human

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:14.408
choice. Approve can authorize one PostgreSQL transaction. Edit loops

00:03:14.408 --> 00:03:18.793
through policy review. Reject must stop without an approved

00:03:18.793 --> 00:03:22.204
write. The prototype never executes a trade.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:28.679
Memory has three roles. Typed graph state exists for

00:03:28.679 --> 00:03:32.454
the run. A thread checkpointer supports pause and resume

00:03:32.454 --> 00:03:36.228
by thread ID. Approved profiles, holdings, decisions, and reports

00:03:36.228 --> 00:03:40.003
live in the repository and appear in History. Pinecone

00:03:40.003 --> 00:03:43.778
stores filing chunks only; it is evidence storage, not

00:03:43.778 --> 00:03:47.552
conversation memory. Service failures retry or use labeled cache,

00:03:47.552 --> 00:03:49.649
while missing evidence remains explicit.

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:56.402
Request edits resumes the interrupted thread, applies reviewer instructions,

00:03:56.402 --> 00:04:00.455
reruns risk review, and returns to the same human

00:04:00.455 --> 00:04:04.508
gate. Failures have deliberate paths: missing inputs request clarification,

00:04:04.508 --> 00:04:08.561
model failures use deterministic fallbacks, specialist errors become structured

00:04:08.561 --> 00:04:12.614
warnings, and persistence failures display as failed rather than

00:04:12.614 --> 00:04:13.515
false success.

00:04:16.215 --> 00:04:19.768
The final decision is Reject. The navigator records rejected

00:04:19.768 --> 00:04:23.321
without a write, and the workspace confirms that no

00:04:23.321 --> 00:04:26.873
write was authorized. This demonstrates the Week 3 framework

00:04:26.873 --> 00:04:30.426
end to end: a supervisor coordinating specialized agents, parallel

00:04:30.426 --> 00:04:33.979
delegation, typed state, bounded tools, visible recovery, and human

00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:37.532
control of the durable action. Success means a reviewable,

00:04:37.532 --> 00:04:41.085
grounded result with correct calculations and zero unapproved writes,

00:04:41.085 --> 00:04:43.453
not simply a convincing model response.
